WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.100 --> 00:06.070
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series

3
00:06.110 --> 00:08.750
are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:08.790 --> 00:13.280
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

5
00:13.320 --> 00:15.720
Viewer discretion is advised.

6
00:16.190 --> 00:17.330
I’ll do everything to find Key.

7
00:17.980 --> 00:18.800
Key.

8
00:19.590 --> 00:22.200
Thank you for saving me.

9
00:22.730 --> 00:23.600
Key, honey.

10
00:24.050 --> 00:26.380
I was the one who made her condition worse.

11
00:26.900 --> 00:28.120
It was my fault.

12
00:28.460 --> 00:30.900
You’re the best dad to me.

13
00:32.220 --> 00:33.970
Are we really going to sleep over here?

14
02:07.520 --> 02:08.550
You can’t sleep?

15
02:14.060 --> 02:14.900
Yes.

16
02:42.770 --> 02:43.800
Are you afraid?

17
02:51.750 --> 02:53.600
I’m afraid that if I fall asleep,

18
02:56.770 --> 02:58.500
I will have a nightmare about my mom.

19
03:03.920 --> 03:05.600
I don’t want to see it again.

20
03:10.270 --> 03:12.040
If you don’t want to have the nightmare again,

21
03:13.640 --> 03:15.580
why don’t we face it together?

22
04:32.040 --> 04:32.800
Key.

23
04:42.620 --> 04:43.600
It’s okay.

24
04:45.780 --> 04:46.600
It’s alright.

25
06:56.740 --> 06:57.900
You are okay now.

26
07:01.660 --> 07:03.290
Everything was just the past.

27
08:36.860 --> 08:37.880
How are you feeling?

28
08:37.919 --> 08:39.400
Did you get a good sleep last night?

29
08:53.000 --> 08:53.850
Mom.

30
08:56.580 --> 08:57.770
I miss you.

31
08:58.650 --> 08:59.980
I’m right here.

32
09:02.520 --> 09:03.960
Do you know…

33
09:05.160 --> 09:06.720
how incredible you are?

34
09:09.330 --> 09:11.400
My daughter is the best.

35
09:14.920 --> 09:16.370
I love you, Mom.

36
09:21.420 --> 09:22.800
I love you, too.

37
09:30.290 --> 09:31.900
So Key,

38
09:32.920 --> 09:34.400
you don’t need to be sad,

39
09:35.460 --> 09:36.800
feel hurt,

40
09:37.620 --> 09:39.500
or feel guilty anymore.

41
09:44.130 --> 09:49.450
The love you gave me made me very happy.

42
09:56.220 --> 09:57.900
Key, promise me.

43
09:59.850 --> 10:02.700
You will go on living a happy life.

44
10:03.720 --> 10:04.780
Can you do that?

45
10:10.970 --> 10:12.100
I promise.

46
10:13.900 --> 10:15.100
I will be happy.

47
10:48.440 --> 10:49.600
You are smiling.

48
10:54.650 --> 10:56.000
Did you have a good dream?

49
10:59.990 --> 11:00.800
Yes.

50
11:02.350 --> 11:03.500
I had a good dream.

51
11:04.300 --> 11:05.500
I dreamt of my mom.

52
11:14.080 --> 11:17.700
I promised her that I would be happy.

53
11:19.830 --> 11:20.800
That’s great.

54
11:25.580 --> 11:27.300
You are my happiness.

55
12:35.450 --> 12:36.500
What did the doctor say?

56
12:37.930 --> 12:40.900
We talked a lot.

57
12:42.460 --> 12:45.100
I haven’t seen a psychiatrist for a while.

58
12:46.250 --> 12:48.200
So I needed to update her about my condition.

59
12:50.200 --> 12:55.500
She said I made the right decision to receive counselling again.

60
12:57.180 --> 12:58.370
In the meantime,

61
12:59.480 --> 13:01.000
I will receive counselling

62
13:02.710 --> 13:05.800
and take the prescribed medication.

63
13:08.240 --> 13:11.150
Did she give you other recommendations?

64
13:12.020 --> 13:14.900
Is there anything that can help you heal?

65
13:18.380 --> 13:21.700
She said that having someone I love,

66
13:22.480 --> 13:24.150
someone who understands me by my side,

67
13:24.730 --> 13:26.200
would be a big help.

68
13:27.320 --> 13:28.600
I already have them.

69
13:29.120 --> 13:32.200
I have you and everyone in my family.

70
13:39.050 --> 13:41.680
Thank you, Chan, for keeping me company today.

71
13:43.170 --> 13:44.100
Company?

72
13:45.310 --> 13:46.400
I’m your girlfriend.

73
13:49.990 --> 13:51.000
Okay.

74
13:51.810 --> 13:54.320
Thank you for being my girlfriend.

75
13:56.970 --> 14:01.000
I will be by your side and stick to you every day.

76
14:02.190 --> 14:04.880
Then I will stick to you

77
14:05.460 --> 14:07.800
like I'm attached to you at the hip.

78
14:15.410 --> 14:17.980
Before we go home, we should go shopping for Simba’s stuff.

79
14:19.650 --> 14:20.480
Sure.

80
14:20.520 --> 14:21.700
What are you going to buy for him?

81
14:24.340 --> 14:25.200
I don’t know.

82
14:25.610 --> 14:27.000
I just want to buy him something.

83
14:29.130 --> 14:31.400
Don’t you want to buy anything for this one?

84
14:34.340 --> 14:35.300
For this one,

85
14:35.830 --> 14:37.730
I’ll take care of her for the rest of my life.

86
14:41.770 --> 14:42.500
Come on.

87
14:42.940 --> 14:43.900
Let’s go shopping.

88
14:44.950 --> 14:45.800
Yeah.

89
15:03.290 --> 15:04.630
Where are you going?

90
15:06.060 --> 15:07.240
I’m going to Paris.

91
15:07.640 --> 15:08.610
I have a shooting there.

92
15:09.300 --> 15:11.100
Didn’t you just come back from Milan?

93
15:11.280 --> 15:12.330
Are you leaving again?

94
15:12.850 --> 15:16.200
When an opportunity comes my way, I have to take it, right?

95
15:17.070 --> 15:18.400
How long will you be away?

96
15:19.360 --> 15:21.500
Around two weeks.

97
15:21.770 --> 15:22.730
Two weeks?

98
15:23.050 --> 15:23.560
Yes.

99
15:23.600 --> 15:25.600
Who am I gonna have to keep me company?

100
15:25.880 --> 15:28.300
You still have Aunt Mam.

101
15:28.630 --> 15:31.340
That’s different. She can’t replace you.

102
15:35.480 --> 15:37.000
It’s nothing personal, Mam.

103
15:38.500 --> 15:39.300
Yes.

104
15:41.730 --> 15:46.450
If you feel lonely, why don’t you find something to do?

105
15:47.190 --> 15:50.210
I’m sure you have many things you want to do,

106
15:50.990 --> 15:54.150
especially meddling in Chan’s life.

107
15:59.890 --> 16:03.200
How could I meddle in her life?

108
16:08.930 --> 16:09.950
Mom.

109
16:10.640 --> 16:14.700
While I’m away, can you please be nice to Chan?

110
16:14.960 --> 16:16.000
I’m asking you.

111
16:16.350 --> 16:17.240
Please.

112
16:23.630 --> 16:25.880
I’ve got to leave now, otherwise I will miss my flight.

113
16:26.590 --> 16:27.330
I’ll see you.

114
16:31.260 --> 16:32.700
Have a safe flight.

115
16:32.870 --> 16:33.530
Yes.

116
16:33.740 --> 16:34.900
I won’t see you off.

117
16:37.270 --> 16:38.300
I’m leaving.

118
16:43.110 --> 16:44.600
Aunt Mam, please take care of my mom.

119
17:15.010 --> 17:16.800
Why do you want me to come with you?

120
17:17.210 --> 17:18.400
It’s so early.

121
17:19.470 --> 17:20.599
I want you to come with me.

122
17:23.859 --> 17:27.200
While waiting for you, I don’t know what to do.

123
17:27.730 --> 17:29.850
I have plenty of time before my band practice at 1 p.m.

124
17:32.390 --> 17:34.500
Just do what you always do when you come to my office.

125
17:36.490 --> 17:37.700
You mean, sitting around?

126
17:40.370 --> 17:41.500
You stare at me.

127
17:44.040 --> 17:44.800
Oh.

128
17:45.500 --> 17:48.300
Did you know that I was staring at you?

129
17:49.750 --> 17:51.100
It would be weird if I didn’t know.

130
17:51.700 --> 17:53.200
You couldn’t stop staring at me.

131
17:56.060 --> 17:58.150
We've always stuck together lately.

132
18:01.840 --> 18:03.400
Then you two should spend some time apart.

133
18:07.160 --> 18:08.150
Mom.

134
18:10.240 --> 18:11.500
Good morning, Madam.

135
18:16.400 --> 18:18.210
Chan, you know what you need to do, right?

136
18:21.250 --> 18:23.400
There’s nothing I need to worry about, right?

137
18:24.850 --> 18:25.700
Yes.

138
18:26.360 --> 18:27.700
Don’t worry, Mom.

139
18:45.630 --> 18:47.100
I’m sorry for my mom.

140
18:49.220 --> 18:50.300
It’s okay.

141
18:51.810 --> 18:53.680
I shouldn’t have told you to come with me.

142
18:56.380 --> 18:59.200
You asked me to come with you because you were worried about me.

143
18:59.750 --> 19:00.650
I know that.

144
19:04.480 --> 19:08.300
About your mom,

145
19:10.160 --> 19:13.800
she is the real last boss, like Sun said.

146
19:18.810 --> 19:22.700
But I believe that you can win her over.

147
19:30.090 --> 19:31.000
Let’s go.

148
19:49.580 --> 19:50.650
I thought

149
19:52.150 --> 19:53.970
you weren’t this kind of person.

150
20:03.790 --> 20:05.450
Do you have something to say to me?

151
20:12.740 --> 20:15.300
You’re not someone who gives up easily.

152
20:18.730 --> 20:20.800
The girl who is standing in front of me

153
20:22.500 --> 20:24.550
is not Jay that I knew.

154
20:25.670 --> 20:27.480
You are not fighting alone.

155
20:29.190 --> 20:30.950
We have the same enemy.

156
20:39.380 --> 20:40.780
So Jay,

157
20:43.560 --> 20:45.100
don’t give up yet.

158
21:36.860 --> 21:37.740
Simba.

159
21:38.040 --> 21:39.700
Mommy and Mama are back.

160
21:44.130 --> 21:45.700
Are you going to sleep over here?

161
21:47.750 --> 21:50.030
Your sister went abroad for work.

162
21:50.900 --> 21:51.800
I feel lonely.

163
21:52.180 --> 21:53.800
So I want to spend time with you.

164
21:57.490 --> 21:59.000
How long are you going to stay?

165
22:01.110 --> 22:02.090
Indefinitely.

166
22:06.090 --> 22:06.930
Whose cat is this?

167
22:10.150 --> 22:11.570
That’s my cat, Mom.

168
22:14.800 --> 22:17.210
I never permitted you to call me Mom.

169
22:24.090 --> 22:25.600
I call you Mom

170
22:26.690 --> 22:29.100
because you are Chan’s Mom.

171
22:29.870 --> 22:31.180
I want to show you respect.

172
22:33.840 --> 22:35.200
You are good at talking back.

173
22:35.240 --> 22:36.290
Mom.

174
22:36.840 --> 22:40.500
If you are going to stay with me, please don’t pick a fight.

175
22:40.540 --> 22:41.400
Why?

176
22:42.250 --> 22:43.730
Are you going to tell me to leave again?

177
22:48.170 --> 22:49.800
I’ll call you Madam.

178
22:51.190 --> 22:55.900
I’ll wait until you are comfortable letting me call you Mom.

179
22:59.410 --> 23:00.600
It’s unlikely to happen.

180
23:04.720 --> 23:05.930
Put the cat somewhere else.

181
23:07.330 --> 23:08.360
I’m allergic to cats.

182
23:09.850 --> 23:11.030
You’ve never had an allergy.

183
23:11.070 --> 23:12.070
Yes, I do.

184
23:13.270 --> 23:14.880
I’m allergic to all kinds of animal fur.

185
23:22.940 --> 23:23.980
I got it.

186
23:24.700 --> 23:29.500
I’ll keep Simba in the bedroom only.

187
23:33.010 --> 23:33.800
Simba.

188
23:35.270 --> 23:36.200
Let's go.

189
23:45.980 --> 23:48.300
I told you to take the cat somewhere else,

190
23:49.180 --> 23:50.880
not to keep it in your bedroom.

191
23:53.070 --> 23:54.490
Where do you want me to take him?

192
23:54.530 --> 23:56.500
Anywhere but here.

193
23:57.250 --> 23:59.250
I told you I’m allergic to animal fur.

194
23:59.390 --> 24:01.180
I’m keeping him only in my room.

195
24:01.220 --> 24:02.380
That’s not enough.

196
24:04.330 --> 24:05.270
Mom.

197
24:06.100 --> 24:07.500
Don’t you feel bad for him?

198
24:11.530 --> 24:12.500
Fine.

199
24:13.250 --> 24:15.400
Don’t let it come near me.

200
24:16.310 --> 24:17.800
I don’t want to see it.

201
24:23.810 --> 24:25.130
Good night, Mom.

202
24:26.380 --> 24:27.500
Good night.

203
24:52.030 --> 24:52.780
Chan.

204
24:54.030 --> 24:55.800
I’m not feeling well.

205
24:56.290 --> 24:57.530
I think I’m going to be sick.

206
24:58.010 --> 24:59.100
You are sick?

207
24:59.980 --> 25:02.030
I’ll call Aunt Mam to come and take care of you.

208
25:02.070 --> 25:03.650
No, it will take too long.

209
25:05.250 --> 25:07.610
I want someone to take care of me right now.

210
25:07.800 --> 25:10.330
Mom, I have to go to work.

211
25:10.490 --> 25:11.500
I know that.

212
25:13.280 --> 25:16.600
But she doesn’t have to go with you.

213
25:24.040 --> 25:25.650
You want me to stay and take care of you?

214
25:27.980 --> 25:29.770
If you have nothing else to do.

215
25:32.210 --> 25:33.720
I only have a schedule this evening.

216
25:34.070 --> 25:35.300
I have to perform with my band.

217
25:37.470 --> 25:38.250
Okay.

218
25:39.010 --> 25:41.970
I’ll have Eggs Benedict, avocado salad,

219
25:42.140 --> 25:44.900
Kyoho grapes, and mineral water for breakfast.

220
25:45.740 --> 25:50.300
For lunch, I want to eat Spanish food.

221
25:50.800 --> 25:52.130
Do you know how to make paella?

222
25:55.560 --> 25:56.600
Mom.

223
25:57.150 --> 25:58.570
You can order it from a restaurant.

224
25:58.890 --> 25:59.980
Why?

225
26:00.470 --> 26:02.200
Can’t you prepare them for me?

226
26:04.150 --> 26:05.210
Of course, I can.

227
26:06.310 --> 26:07.500
No problem.

228
26:08.050 --> 26:09.100
Mom.

229
26:10.630 --> 26:12.300
Oops, I mean, Madam.

230
26:30.040 --> 26:32.380
I don’t want to leave you alone with Mom.

231
26:35.720 --> 26:36.800
It’s okay.

232
26:37.590 --> 26:38.700
Don’t worry about me.

233
26:40.950 --> 26:44.200
I think my mom must be up to something.

234
26:46.150 --> 26:47.200
I know.

235
26:48.050 --> 26:49.550
I also have something up my sleeve.

236
26:51.410 --> 26:52.400
What is it?

237
26:55.020 --> 26:56.100
I can’t tell you.

238
26:58.970 --> 27:00.600
Will you two end up fighting again?

239
27:01.870 --> 27:04.530
I think I should take leave today.

240
27:05.490 --> 27:06.500
Don’t do that.

241
27:07.040 --> 27:09.140
Even if you took leave, your mom wouldn’t leave me alone.

242
27:09.870 --> 27:14.370
It would give her a chance to criticize you.

243
27:16.500 --> 27:17.900
I’m worried about you.

244
27:22.940 --> 27:24.000
You should go to work.

245
27:31.090 --> 27:31.900
Fine.

246
27:36.560 --> 27:37.400
Bye.

247
28:23.670 --> 28:24.600
What’s up, Phu?

248
28:29.530 --> 28:32.210
Every time you have that look on your face when you come to see me,

249
28:33.470 --> 28:34.600
it’s always about Jay.

250
28:37.700 --> 28:38.900
You’re right.

251
28:41.510 --> 28:43.050
I told you.

252
28:43.640 --> 28:46.400
If it’s about Jay, I don’t want to hear it.

253
28:55.740 --> 28:57.500
Can you hear me out this time?

254
29:00.900 --> 29:02.700
I won’t bother you about this again.

255
29:07.000 --> 29:08.600
I came to tell you about Jay

256
29:10.590 --> 29:11.920
because I feel bad for her.

257
29:13.740 --> 29:15.570
I’ve never seen her in such a wreck.

258
29:16.900 --> 29:18.400
She is a complete mess.

259
29:20.390 --> 29:21.300
I think,

260
29:22.790 --> 29:24.670
for the sake of our long friendship,

261
29:26.380 --> 29:27.750
can you go talk to her?

262
29:29.540 --> 29:31.410
So you won’t have anything unresolved between you two.

263
29:35.090 --> 29:37.100
Jay wants to talk to you one last time.

264
30:34.520 --> 30:36.850
I’m glad that you came to see me.

265
30:41.130 --> 30:43.800
Phu told me you wanted to talk to me.

266
30:45.430 --> 30:46.300
What is it?

267
30:54.280 --> 30:55.500
If…

268
31:00.890 --> 31:02.770
I hadn’t left you back then,

269
31:05.540 --> 31:10.300
what do you think we’d be like now?

270
31:13.370 --> 31:17.630
Would we still love each other?

271
31:18.810 --> 31:23.300
Would we get married and have our happy ending?

272
31:29.090 --> 31:30.400
Please say something.

273
31:46.130 --> 31:47.600
Our relationship,

274
31:51.380 --> 31:52.700
it’s too late.

275
31:54.820 --> 31:56.000
The thing that you said,

276
31:58.490 --> 31:59.980
it will never happen.

277
32:01.490 --> 32:02.700
You and I,

278
32:03.580 --> 32:05.100
we are not in love anymore.

279
32:11.680 --> 32:13.300
Everything about us is just the past.

280
32:15.880 --> 32:17.500
I want you to move on.

281
32:25.380 --> 32:26.700
You need to focus on the present.

282
32:29.820 --> 32:32.200
But I want to have you in my present.

283
32:36.640 --> 32:37.760
No, Jay.

284
32:38.060 --> 32:41.400
You and I can only be friends.

285
32:43.260 --> 32:45.300
But I don’t want to be your friend.

286
32:58.840 --> 33:01.180
This is the last time that we talk.

287
33:08.210 --> 33:09.200
You know what?

288
33:14.060 --> 33:16.700
I never thought I could be such a loser.

289
33:26.590 --> 33:28.500
Then go back to being the old you.

290
33:51.120 --> 33:53.700
Can you give me another chance?

291
34:00.260 --> 34:02.550
You’re asking for something I can’t give you.

292
34:06.320 --> 34:07.600
I really love Key.

293
34:23.540 --> 34:25.000
Are you sure?

294
34:35.030 --> 34:35.900
Jay.

295
34:37.179 --> 34:41.500
I think our love is better left as a memory.

296
34:45.639 --> 34:46.900
I want you…

297
34:48.920 --> 34:51.199
to remember only the good memories about us.

298
34:56.150 --> 34:58.700
Even though our love has ended,

299
35:02.240 --> 35:03.840
I don’t want it to be ruined.

300
35:09.610 --> 35:11.100
I can put myself back together.

301
35:12.610 --> 35:14.000
So can you.

302
35:17.160 --> 35:20.660
Jay that I knew, she can definitely do it.

303
35:56.480 --> 35:58.100
Be careful.

304
36:05.200 --> 36:06.300
Your mom…

305
36:09.310 --> 36:11.200
will never accept Key.

306
36:17.260 --> 36:18.300
Thank you.

307
37:27.530 --> 37:28.760
Why did you stop walking?

308
37:29.980 --> 37:31.120
Did I forget something?

309
37:34.220 --> 37:35.200
Forgot what?

310
37:36.210 --> 37:38.000
I’m asking you.

311
37:42.960 --> 37:44.250
Did you forget your bag?

312
37:44.580 --> 37:46.900
Where did you leave it?

313
37:47.610 --> 37:49.070
Where do you think I left it?

314
37:52.340 --> 37:53.330
In the car?

315
37:53.640 --> 37:55.180
Then go check it.

316
37:57.640 --> 38:01.290
I’ll put these bags in the room first. Then I’ll go down to check it.

317
38:01.540 --> 38:02.380
No.

318
38:04.160 --> 38:05.170
You need to go check it right now.

319
38:06.860 --> 38:08.730
Can you take these bags to the room?

320
38:09.330 --> 38:10.200
No.

321
38:11.030 --> 38:12.800
I’m tired. I’ll go wait in the room.

322
38:15.540 --> 38:17.700
Why don’t you take these bags with you?

323
38:18.570 --> 38:19.890
I’ll go check your bag in the car.

324
38:20.490 --> 38:21.370
Please.

325
38:25.300 --> 38:26.100
No.

326
38:55.020 --> 38:56.400
Why did it take you so long?

327
38:56.440 --> 38:57.900
I almost don’t want to wait anymore.

328
38:59.550 --> 39:00.800
I’m sorry to keep you waiting.

329
39:06.730 --> 39:08.600
It looks similar to the original recipe.

330
39:10.180 --> 39:10.900
Yes.

331
39:11.600 --> 39:14.290
I cooked it for my family before.

332
39:15.690 --> 39:16.550
Really?

333
39:17.850 --> 39:19.170
Did they eat it?

334
39:20.340 --> 39:22.000
They said it was delicious.

335
39:22.630 --> 39:24.300
I learned it from a talented chef.

336
39:27.310 --> 39:29.360
Did you hire a chef from Spain to teach you?

337
39:30.650 --> 39:31.500
No.

338
39:31.780 --> 39:32.900
I learned from Chef Niam,

339
39:33.550 --> 39:35.330
a house helper who works for my family.

340
39:35.370 --> 39:36.700
She is an amazing cook.

341
39:37.150 --> 39:38.800
She learned the recipe from YouTube.

342
39:43.110 --> 39:45.400
If it doesn’t taste good, I won’t eat it.

343
39:46.890 --> 39:48.490
Yes, me too.

344
40:11.710 --> 40:12.600
How is it?

345
40:13.930 --> 40:16.400
Does it suit your palate, Mom?

346
40:18.890 --> 40:20.500
I mean, Madam.

347
40:42.750 --> 40:45.130
May I be excused to check on Simba?

348
41:32.230 --> 41:33.400
What are you doing?

349
41:34.740 --> 41:36.370
Why don’t you read my message?

350
41:49.420 --> 41:50.570
What are they doing?

351
42:15.470 --> 42:17.800
Mom, you seem to enjoy your meal.

352
42:20.440 --> 42:21.800
Where is Key?

353
42:23.550 --> 42:25.200
You smell so good.

354
42:31.920 --> 42:33.190
(What are you doing, hooman?)

355
42:36.410 --> 42:37.450
Key.

356
42:41.370 --> 42:42.700
I’m watching our cat.

357
42:44.110 --> 42:45.200
Meow.

358
42:45.870 --> 42:46.970
Meow, meow.

359
42:47.690 --> 42:49.700
(Do your best at work, hooman.)

360
42:54.160 --> 42:56.640
This cat is quite something.

361
42:57.580 --> 42:58.800
(Good luck with work.)

362
43:00.020 --> 43:00.900
(Meow.)

363
43:45.160 --> 43:45.900
Shit.

364
43:46.290 --> 43:47.300
Again?

365
43:48.490 --> 43:49.300
Yes.

366
43:49.810 --> 43:50.950
You got drunk again.

367
44:01.660 --> 44:03.600
You are wearing my pajamas.

368
44:04.130 --> 44:05.630
Please wash before returning.

369
44:11.060 --> 44:12.300
What happened last night?

370
44:15.450 --> 44:16.490
Do you really want to know?

371
44:24.860 --> 44:26.280
Don’t you remember…

372
44:28.610 --> 44:30.100
what we did?

373
44:49.860 --> 44:50.600
Elle.

374
44:53.040 --> 44:53.840
Hi, Phu.

375
45:00.360 --> 45:01.800
Did you follow me?

376
45:03.350 --> 45:04.400
Calm down, Jay.

377
45:05.290 --> 45:06.600
I invited her.

378
45:08.780 --> 45:10.000
Why didn’t you tell me sooner?

379
45:12.080 --> 45:13.250
So I would go to another bar.

380
45:13.890 --> 45:15.100
Wait.

381
45:16.020 --> 45:17.600
Why do you keep running away from me?

382
45:21.570 --> 45:22.500
No, I don’t.

383
45:24.170 --> 45:25.400
Are you…

384
45:26.430 --> 45:27.300
having feelings for me?

385
45:35.610 --> 45:36.800
No way.

386
45:37.890 --> 45:39.400
Then let’s have a drink together.

387
45:41.540 --> 45:42.570
Are you asking me out on a date?

388
45:44.010 --> 45:44.840
Yes.

389
45:46.300 --> 45:48.320
It’s a friend date.

390
45:50.380 --> 45:51.600
Nothing romantic.

391
45:52.980 --> 45:54.600
Nothing…

392
45:55.810 --> 45:56.700
sexual.

393
46:02.280 --> 46:04.150
Can I have a strong Vodka?

394
46:10.440 --> 46:11.400
Do you dare?

395
46:15.440 --> 46:16.700
I thought you would dare.

396
46:34.860 --> 46:36.850
You live up to your reputation, Miss Boozer.

397
46:39.520 --> 46:40.780
Can I have another glass?

398
47:23.830 --> 47:25.030
I don’t get it.

399
47:26.020 --> 47:27.580
What is so special about that girl?

400
47:27.810 --> 47:29.600
Why is Chan so devoted to her?

401
47:31.450 --> 47:33.000
It’s no longer your business.

402
47:34.690 --> 47:36.120
Why are you worried about Chan?

403
47:38.240 --> 47:40.500
How can I not be worried about her?

404
47:41.050 --> 47:42.560
Look at what she’s doing.

405
47:44.610 --> 47:47.100
But she doesn’t want you to fuss over her.

406
47:48.740 --> 47:51.000
What Chat does is no longer your business.

407
47:55.300 --> 47:57.400
The only thing that you can do right now…

408
48:05.890 --> 48:06.850
is have a drink.

409
48:40.550 --> 48:43.000
I secretly did some digging on you.

410
48:47.250 --> 48:51.800
You are a well-known pilot.

411
48:53.250 --> 48:56.240
You are the most talented female pilot in your class.

412
49:00.750 --> 49:03.400
You like secretly dating flight attendants.

413
49:06.290 --> 49:08.630
Who knows how many airlines you’ve dated by now?

414
49:27.820 --> 49:29.750
I’m not a flight attendant.

415
49:33.920 --> 49:36.700
But are you interested in keeping me company tonight?

416
49:55.650 --> 50:00.930
So you and I,

417
50:04.590 --> 50:05.920
did we sleep together?

418
50:16.800 --> 50:17.700
No way.

419
50:18.750 --> 50:20.270
Why don’t I remember anything?

420
50:20.310 --> 50:22.090
I remember that we were in a nightclub.

421
50:22.430 --> 50:24.200
Then I blacked out.

422
50:28.690 --> 50:29.780
Why are you laughing?

423
50:31.280 --> 50:32.200
Listen.

424
50:33.040 --> 50:35.000
Since the day you first met me,

425
50:35.630 --> 50:37.800
the closest that we got was

426
50:41.600 --> 50:44.120
when you rolled over to hold me before you woke up.

427
50:45.160 --> 50:47.040
Nothing happened between us.

428
50:47.080 --> 50:49.100
Because I rejected you.

429
50:50.070 --> 50:51.770
After that, you got wasted

430
50:51.880 --> 50:53.940
and threw up on the side of the road again.

431
50:54.290 --> 50:56.300
So I needed to take you back to my room.

432
50:56.950 --> 50:58.600
I changed your clothes.

433
51:00.110 --> 51:02.370
Then I put you into the bed because I felt sorry for you.

434
51:02.640 --> 51:03.540
Do you get it now?

435
51:03.580 --> 51:04.370
That’s not true.

436
51:04.480 --> 51:07.130
Sorry, but it’s true, darling.

437
51:07.950 --> 51:10.430
You should go take a shower. Then I’ll give you a ride home.

438
51:12.860 --> 51:14.160
Why will you give me a ride home?

439
51:14.700 --> 51:16.780
When you get drunk next time,

440
51:17.210 --> 51:19.000
I’ll know where to drop you off.

441
51:19.890 --> 51:23.100
So you won’t have to sleep over here, honey.

442
51:27.490 --> 51:28.900
Or do you want me to help you take a shower?

443
51:28.940 --> 51:29.800
Come here.

444
51:30.870 --> 51:33.590
-You weren’t resisting last night. -No.

445
52:04.610 --> 52:06.100
Aren’t you going to say thank you?

446
52:13.740 --> 52:15.100
Thank you for giving me a ride.

447
52:19.310 --> 52:21.100
Do you want to get a cup of coffee tomorrow?

448
52:22.930 --> 52:24.330
Are you asking me out on a date?

449
52:28.950 --> 52:30.400
It’s just friends hanging out.

450
52:31.800 --> 52:32.700
No?

451
52:34.490 --> 52:36.800
Are you having feelings for me?

452
52:39.080 --> 52:39.820
Is that a joke?

453
52:39.860 --> 52:41.080
I have no feelings for you.

454
52:42.350 --> 52:43.180
So?

455
52:43.940 --> 52:45.020
Are you going?

456
52:46.110 --> 52:47.730
If you say no, I’ll go ask someone else.

457
52:52.150 --> 52:53.640
My answer is no.

458
52:53.930 --> 52:55.180
Do whatever you want.

459
52:56.370 --> 52:58.100
Okay. I got it.

460
52:58.830 --> 53:00.800
Have a nice day, Miss Jay.

461
53:06.100 --> 53:08.000
That’s it? Aren’t you going to try a little harder?

462
53:15.560 --> 53:16.670
What the f*ck!

463
53:59.050 --> 54:00.600
Don’t drag this out.

464
54:00.940 --> 54:02.400
You’ll only end up hurting more.

465
54:04.400 --> 54:05.500
I agree.

466
54:05.970 --> 54:09.600
You should come to terms with Chan’s decision.

467
54:10.260 --> 54:14.800
No matter what, I will never break up with Chan.

468
54:18.960 --> 54:20.000
Can I ask you something?

469
54:21.130 --> 54:23.300
Do you really think Chan will choose you over me?

470
54:26.440 --> 54:28.500
She doesn’t need to choose.

471
54:30.120 --> 54:31.800
She can have us both.

472
54:33.400 --> 54:34.300
Is that so?

473
54:35.750 --> 54:38.370
We are only going to take our hatred out on each other.

474
54:39.830 --> 54:41.100
It will be very toxic.

475
54:41.830 --> 54:43.270
Don’t you feel sorry for Chan?

476
54:46.750 --> 54:49.050
Why do we have to hate each other?

477
54:54.330 --> 54:55.170
No way.

478
55:20.240 --> 55:21.200
Mom.

479
55:27.250 --> 55:28.570
I love you.

480
55:32.920 --> 55:34.780
I invited you to join me today.

481
55:37.520 --> 55:39.300
Because I want you to be present

482
55:41.640 --> 55:44.100
in the most important moment of my life.

483
56:45.390 --> 56:47.400
I will use these earrings

484
56:50.770 --> 56:52.400
to propose to you.

485
57:00.680 --> 57:02.200
Will you marry me, Key?

486
57:42.020 --> 57:45.100
Your mom will never accept me.

487
57:45.560 --> 57:46.730
Don’t give up yet.

488
57:47.180 --> 57:48.250
Don’t leave me.

489
57:48.660 --> 57:50.570
I will never give up on us.

490
57:51.630 --> 57:53.500
I want you to stop holding on to it.

491
57:53.820 --> 57:55.520
If you keep doing this,

492
57:55.800 --> 57:57.700
you may end up losing Chan as a friend.

493
57:58.540 --> 57:59.300
Simba.

494
58:00.010 --> 58:01.880
I don’t know where Mom took Simba.

495
58:02.210 --> 58:04.280
I checked the camera. I didn’t see anyone home.

496
58:04.510 --> 58:09.330
I’m afraid that Mom is willing to do anything to win.

497
58:10.900 --> 58:12.240
Honey.

498
58:12.280 --> 58:13.570
What do you want to talk to me about?

499
58:14.020 --> 58:15.570
Key is the only one I will marry.

500
58:15.840 --> 58:18.210
If you want me to accept your marriage,

501
58:18.660 --> 58:20.530
then you need to give me something in exchange.
